orrectly reconstruct child process args when server started via `python -m custom_module runserver`. Current logic uses __main__.__spec__.parent, which drops last segment of dotted module when entry is module (foo.bar.baz). Need to preserve full module specced for -m. Tests in test_autoreload.py cover various cases including non-django module module. We must change get_child_arguments accordingly.\"},{\"id\":\"phase2\",\"title\":\"Run test suite to see failures related to autoreloader\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"id\":\"phase3\",\"title\":\"Explore repository to locate autoreloader code and -m handling\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase4\",\"title\":\"Create minimal reproduction script to simulate python -m module runserver scenario\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase5\",\"title\":\"Analyze fix approach and determine minimal code changes\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase6\",\"title\":\"Implement code changes in repository\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase7\",\"title\":\"Verify fix with reproduction and run affected tests\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase8\",\"title\":\"Final review against issue requirements and base commit\",\"status\":\"todo\"}]}"}}]}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Task list has been updated with 8 items. Stored in session directory: sessions/8a779640-a0f9-49-2eb849f3f7ad13d/TASKS.md"}], "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_QDfXJVFlqRGoSN0Gk3Js9wGy", "name": "task_tracker"}, {"content": [], "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_kI5RnkUZmXUnzTBVI2vPlQDo", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cd tests && python -m pip install -e .. && python -m pip install -r requirements/py3.txt\",\"timeout\":1200,\"security_risk\":\"MEDIUM\"}"}}]}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Obtaining file:///workspace/django__django__4.0\n  Installing build dependencies ... done\n  Checking if build backend supports build_editable ... done\n  Getting requirements to build e